  "He was handicapped from childhood and could not walk without assistance.|||From an early age, the boy suffered a severe injury to his left leg after a fall from a stone embankment near his village. The injury never healed properly, leaving him with a permanent limp and frequent pain. Throughout his childhood, he relied heavily on wooden crutches crafted by his father, and long journeys were rare. Villagers often remarked on how slowly he moved and how easily he became exhausted. Physical labor was difficult for him, and he was usually assigned sedentary tasks while others worked the fields.": false,
  "He was handicapped from childhood and could not walk without assistance.|||Despite his difficult upbringing, there came a summer when he discovered an old bicycle abandoned near the riverbank. Over the following weeks, he began cycling every morning along the dirt paths that connected neighboring villages. He rode for miles without stopping, enjoying the freedom of movement the bicycle gave him. By the end of the season, he was known among traders for arriving swiftly, often ahead of those traveling on foot or by cart.": false,
  "He was handicapped from childhood and could not walk without assistance.|||On the day of the autumn festival, he walked through the crowded marketplace unaided, weaving between stalls and greeting familiar faces. Witnesses later recalled how he stood for hours listening to musicians and strolling casually through the square, showing no visible signs of discomfort as he moved from one end of the town to the other.": false,
