  "He was handicapped from childhood and could not walk without assistance.|||As he grew older, friends frequently helped him travel between neighboring settlements by pulling his cart along the dirt paths. While others walked or rode animals, he remained seated, grateful for their assistance. Long-distance travel was rare and carefully planned, as uneven ground caused him discomfort and fatigue. He never attempted journeys alone, knowing his physical limitations.": false,
  "He was handicapped from childhood and could not walk without assistance.|||During the autumn festival, he spent most of the day seated near the marketplace, watching the crowds pass by. Friends brought him food and news from across the square, and musicians occasionally gathered nearby so he could listen without having to move. Witnesses remembered him smiling warmly from his place, rarely changing position and always relying on others for help when relocating.": false,
  "He was handicapped from childhood and could not walk without assistance.|||That evening, as lanterns were lit and songs echoed softly through the streets, he reflected quietly on the life he had learned to accept. Though hardship had shaped much of his youth, he found comfort in companionship and the kindness of those who stood beside him whenever he needed help.": false,
  "He had never left his hometown until adulthood.|||The boy spent his early years in the quiet routines of his hometown, growing familiar with its narrow streets and familiar faces. Life followed a predictable pattern, shaped by seasons and local customs. He was known to many, and little about him seemed to change from one year to the next.": false,
  "He had never left his hometown until adulthood.|||At a young age, he was selected to receive formal instruction at the Eastern Academy, an institution renowned for training scholars and administrators. Each term, he studied under senior instructors, learning subjects unavailable in his hometown. The journey was demanding, and the separation from familiar surroundings required discipline and adjustment.": false,
  "He had never left his hometown until adulthood.|||Over the following years, his education continued uninterrupted. He became accustomed to life within the academy’s stone halls, lodging alongside other students and adhering to schedules far stricter than those of his childhood. Letters from home arrived irregularly, often delayed by weather or road conditions.": false,
  "He had never left his hometown until adulthood.|||During seasonal recesses, he did not return immediately, choosing instead to remain where his studies were conducted. Time passed in steady cycles of work and examination, until eventually he reached adulthood with a perspective shaped by years of structured training and exposure beyond his earliest environment.": false,
